{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass after these things.</b> Rashi explained: after the words of the Satan etc. And one says: after the words of Yishmael. What Rashi explained is as it is, because we say in general: every place where 'after' is said it means immediately adjacent, but here we cannot say so as Rashi explained here. And that year preceded the binding of Yitzchak by twelve years. And one says <b>after these things</b> — after Avraham cut a covenant with Avimelech, to him and to his grandson and to his great-grandson, without permission from HaKadosh Baruch Hu, and the land of the Philistines was given to him and to his seed, as it is written: 'and I will set your border from the Sea of Reeds to the sea of the Philistines,' and also in Joshua all the cities of the five lords of the Philistines are listed within the entire border of the land of Israel, and HaKadosh Baruch Hu commanded them: 'you shall not let any soul live.' Therefore 'and the Elohim tested Avraham' — He goaded him and distressed him, the language of 'in their testing of YHWH,' 'massah and merivah'; and 'the wrathful are called' is translated 'nissin,' with the nun and the same root as 'veniso' in Daniel — meaning: you grew proud through the son I gave you, to cut a covenant between you and between their sons; now go and bring him up as a burnt offering, and you will see what the cutting of the covenant availed. Another interpretation: <b>tested Avraham</b> — the language of testing; and He did not test him for His own sake, for everything is revealed and known before Him — what was, what is, and what will be — but He brought him to the point of trial before the attribute of justice, which was prosecuting against him, and to make known to the creatures how fully his heart volunteered to do the will of his Creator, so that they would not be able to prosecute against him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase 'הנם זועפים מתורגם נסיסים' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The reference appears to be to Onkelos or Targum on a verse where wrathful/angry ones are rendered with a root related to נסס, possibly connected to Daniel 3:19 'וסאמא' (His appearance darkened/wrathful)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:21.400180842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}